<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spartacus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 71 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Spartacus was a Thracian gladiator who led the largest slave revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a>, the Third Servile War of 73–71 BCE. Escaping from a gladiator school at Capua with about seventy companions, he gathered an army of tens of thousands and defeated several Roman forces across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. He was killed in battle against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus">Marcus Licinius Crassus</a> in 71 BCE, and thousands of captured rebels were crucified along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appian-way">Appian Way</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spartacus.jpg" alt="Spartacus" width="320" height="552" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carole Raddato from FRANKFURT, Germany · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%CE%A3%CF%80%CE%AC%CF%81%CF%84%CE%B1%CE%BA%CE%BF%CF%82_Spartacus,Espartaco_marble_statue_in_Louvre_%22%CE%9C%CE%B1%CE%B9%CE%B4%CE%BF%CE%B9_clan_-Meadow%22_slave_macedon-greek.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
